1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,406
The Great Pancake Flip.

3
00:00:03,406 --> 00:00:05,760
Sunday breakfast smells wonderful.

4
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:09,812
Mom is making pancakes, and I've decided I'm old enough to help with the pan.

5
00:00:09,812 --> 00:00:12,698
Ben has decided he's old enough to help with the eating.

6
00:00:12,698 --> 00:00:14,510
Very different jobs.

7
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:16,146
Can you show me how?

8
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:17,591
Sure.

9
00:00:17,591 --> 00:00:21,039
Stand beside me, and keep the pan handle turned inward.

10
00:00:21,039 --> 00:00:23,112
I'll help you with the hot pan.

11
00:00:23,112 --> 00:00:26,007
You can start by pouring a small circle of batter.

12
00:00:26,284 --> 00:00:29,174
I pour a circle that looks more like a sleepy cloud.

13
00:00:29,174 --> 00:00:31,632
We watch little bubbles appear on top.

14
00:00:31,632 --> 00:00:33,205
Is it ready to flip?

15
00:00:33,484 --> 00:00:34,728
Almost.

16
00:00:34,728 --> 00:00:36,936
Wait until the edges look set.

17
00:00:36,936 --> 00:00:39,342
Then slide the spatula underneath.

18
00:00:39,628 --> 00:00:42,192
I believe in you, pancake cloud.

19
00:00:42,412 --> 00:00:45,156
I try to turn it, but one edge folds over.

20
00:00:45,156 --> 00:00:48,343
It lands looking like a blanket that someone forgot to straighten.

21
00:00:48,628 --> 00:00:49,986
That's okay.

22
00:00:49,986 --> 00:00:51,945
Let's try a smaller one.

23
00:00:51,945 --> 00:00:54,830
The first pancake can be a practice pancake.

24
00:00:55,108 --> 00:00:57,829
I volunteer to test the practice pancake.

25
00:00:58,060 --> 00:01:01,314
This time, I pour less batter and wait a little longer.

26
00:01:01,314 --> 00:01:04,595
Mom steadies the pan while I slide the spatula underneath.

27
00:01:04,595 --> 00:01:07,627
One careful turn, and the pancake lands flat.

28
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:09,144
Beautiful.

29
00:01:09,144 --> 00:01:11,227
A round breakfast miracle.

30
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:12,952
Nicely done.

31
00:01:12,952 --> 00:01:15,796
I'll finish cooking these while you two set the table.

32
00:01:16,084 --> 00:01:19,182
We bring plates, forks, and fruit to the table.

33
00:01:19,182 --> 00:01:22,369
Ben gets the folded pancake, just as he requested.

34
00:01:22,369 --> 00:01:26,442
He takes a bite and announces that it tastes exactly like a successful pancake.

35
00:01:26,442 --> 00:01:28,776
It simply has a more interesting shape.
